      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "This study demonstrates that ionizable lipids with a pKa between 6.0 and 6.5 maximize lipoplex stability at physiological pH while triggering critical membrane fusionevents during the endosomal acidification phase. By precisely tuning amino-concentration and pKa to facilitate rapid protonation and electrostatic collapse, these optimized lipids effectively disrupt endosomal membranes, preventing lysosomal degradation and ensuring robust cytosolic mRNA translocation. Consequently, this mechanistic refinement yields a fourfold enhancement in protein expression levels, directly correlating structural lipid parameters with the therapeutic window of mRNA-based vaccines.",
